<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis Light</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1740">1740</a>–<a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis Light was a British trader and naval officer who founded the British settlement on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a> in 1786. He obtained the island from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Abdullah of Kedah on behalf of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, implying military protection that the company never gave. He named the island <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> Island and founded George Town as a free port, serving as superintendent until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-light.jpg" alt="Francis Light" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pangalau · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Cornwallis,_Penang_2023_09.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
